# Secrets for {{ app }} in UAT

Sealed secrets go in this folder. Each one can only be opened by the cluster, and only as
that Secret name in namespace `{{ app }}-uat`. Values are piped into the sealing script and
never appear on a command line, on screen or in Git. Run from the root of GitOps-Repo.

| Secret | Keys | Who provides the values |
|---|---|---|
| `ghcr-pull` | `.dockerconfigjson` | Platform team (registry read token) |
{%- if backend != 'none' %}
| `backend-secrets` | `DATABASE_URL`, `JWT_SECRET`{% if needs_redis %}, `REDIS_URL`{% endif %}{% if needs_kafka %}, `KAFKA_PASSWORD`{% endif %} and every other secret the backend reads | The app's secret owners (readiness rule A18) |
{%- endif %}
{%- if worker %}
| `{{ worker }}-secrets` | `DATABASE_URL`{% if needs_kafka %}, `KAFKA_PASSWORD`{% endif %} (only what the worker needs) | The app's secret owners |
{%- endif %}

```sh
# Registry pull secret (a token with ONLY read:packages)
read -rsp 'token: ' t; echo
printf '.dockerconfigjson={"auths":{"ghcr.io":{"auth":"%s"}}}\n' "$(printf '%s' "bot:$t" | base64 -w0)" \
  | ./scripts/seal-secret.sh {{ app }} uat ghcr-pull kubernetes.io/dockerconfigjson
{% if backend != 'none' %}
# Backend secrets (one KEY=VALUE per line; add every variable the app reads)
printf 'DATABASE_URL=%s\nJWT_SECRET=%s\n' "$db_url" "$(openssl rand -hex 32)" \
  | ./scripts/seal-secret.sh {{ app }} uat backend-secrets
{% endif %}
{%- if worker %}
printf 'DATABASE_URL=%s\n' "$db_url" | ./scripts/seal-secret.sh {{ app }} uat {{ worker }}-secrets
{% endif %}
```

Lab services (`scripts/lab-services.sh`) create the database{% if needs_redis %}, the Redis user{% endif %}{% if needs_kafka %} and the Kafka user{% endif %}
from `{{ app | upper | replace('-', '_') }}_UAT_DB_PASSWORD`{% if needs_redis %}, `..._REDIS_PASSWORD`{% endif %}{% if needs_kafka %}, `..._KAFKA_PASSWORD`{% endif %} in
team-secrets. At RSSB these are requests to the database{% if needs_redis %}, Redis{% endif %}{% if needs_kafka %} and Kafka{% endif %} owners (infra-ops forms).

Delete this file once the secrets are sealed, or keep it as the inventory.
